<title>GERMANY: UK encouraged by Kohl comments on Eurofighter.</title>
<headline>UK encouraged by Kohl comments on Eurofighter.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Chancellor Helmut Kohl told visiting British Prime Minister Tony Blair on Friday that he continues to believe the Eurofighter is needed and wants a decision on it to be taken soon, British officials said.</p>
<p>Briefing reporters after talks between Blair and Kohl, the officials said the British leader was &quot;extremely pleased&quot; with Kohl's comments.</p>
<p>Kohl told Blair that he hoped a decision on the funding of the production stage of the project could made in the weeks ahead, they added.</p>
<p>The jet is being jointly developed in a four-nation project by Daimler-Benz Aerospce AG, British Aerospace, Spain's CASA and Italy's Alenia.</p>
<p>Thousands of jobs, particularly British, are seen as depending on the project going ahead.</p>
<p>--Bonn Newsroom +49 228 260 97 160</p>
